  "ai_language_tip": "Use Dutch (nl); English is very widely understood and many businesses switch readily, but start in Dutch for clinics, municipal offices and trades.",
  "english_ok": "yes — Most staff in cities speak good English; still less common at small-town GP practices, trades and with older staff.",
  "politeness": "Direct, efficient and informal-polite: 'u' with strangers on the phone, quickly moving to 'je' in casual venues; open with 'Goedemiddag, u spreekt met …' style; get to the point; close with 'Dank u wel, fijne dag'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings 'op naam van …' (surname); surnames with prefixes (van, de, van der) are filed under the main part in some systems, so spell the full form clearly; Dutch phonetic spelling alphabet uses city/first names.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 06 then 8 digits (e.g. 06 12345678), landline 0XX XXX XXXX (Amsterdam 020); international +31; WhatsApp and SMS confirmations common.",
  "time_tip": "CRITICAL: 'half acht' = 7:30 (half to eight)! Also 'vijf voor half acht' = 7:25 and 'tien over half acht' = 7:40; written 24h ('19.30 uur'); always read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Mobile numbers read as 06 then pairs or 4-4; Dutch says units before tens ('vierentwintig' = 24) like German.",
  "avoid_calling": "Call GPs in the morning slot (often 8:00–10:00) for same-day appointments; avoid restaurant peak 18:00–20:00 and calls after 21:00; Sunday for non-hospitality.",
  "closed_days": "Many shops open Sunday afternoon in cities (koopzondag); many restaurants closed Monday (and sometimes Tuesday); GP practices closed weekends (huisartsenpost for urgent care); holidays include King's Day (27 April), Easter Monday, Ascension, Whit Monday, Christmas.",
  "booking_channels": "Phone for GPs (assistant triage) plus practice apps/portals; TheFork and Formitable-powered venue widgets for restaurants; Treatwell and Salonized-type widgets for salons; Thuisbezorgd and Uber Eats for delivery; phone still normal for trades and small businesses.",
  "voice_menu": "GP practices commonly start with a phone menu (option 1 for urgent), as do banks, telecoms (KPN, Odido, VodafoneZiggo), PostNL and municipalities; restaurants answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Online bookings send e-mail/SMS confirmations; GP assistants call back after triage; trades often reply by WhatsApp.",
